course: dictionary
lesson: 11397
title: Places to stay and fair arrangements
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Accommodation is a place to live or stay, such as a house, a flat or a hotel room. When people go on holiday, they book accommodation before they travel. «We found cheap accommodation by the sea for our summer holiday.» The word tells you where they will sleep.
explain: Accommodation can also be a sum of money in a budget problem. «The hotel costs £60 a night, so 3 nights of accommodation cost £180.» Check the clues: a night is one price, and 3 nights means 3 times that price.
explain: Sometimes accommodation means an agreement that helps both sides. «The school and the parents reached an accommodation that suited everyone.» Nobody lost, and both sides got what they needed. This is a formal use, so it is more common in grown-up writing.
explain: In US schools, accommodations (with an s) means changes that help a pupil learn. «Maya's teacher gave her extra time in tests as an accommodation.» Read the clues: extra time helps a pupil with special needs, so the word is about help, not a place to stay.
fact: Accommodation means a place to live or stay, such as a house, flat or hotel room.
fact: In the UK, accommodation is usually uncountable: you say «some accommodation», not «two accommodations».
fact: In the formal sense, accommodation means an agreement or arrangement that helps both sides.
fact: In US schools, accommodations means changes that help a pupil learn, like extra time.
fact: Useful phrases: holiday accommodation, student accommodation, find accommodation.
exercise: «We need to find accommodation for the night.» What does accommodation mean here? | A type of maths sum | A school test | A kind of holiday food | *A place to stay
exercise: The hotel costs £60 a night. What do 3 nights of accommodation cost? | *£180 | £63 | £120 | £200
exercise: In US schools, what are changes that help a pupil learn, like extra time, called? | Lessons | Bookings | Holidays | *Accommodations
test: «The two sides reached an accommodation that suited both of them.» What does accommodation mean in this sentence? | *An agreement that helps both sides | A school test | Money paid to a hotel | A large house
test: Which phrase means a place for students to live? | Lesson plan | Holiday accommodation | Maths budget | *Student accommodation
exam: Which sentence uses accommodation correctly in the UK? | We booked two accommodations for a week by the sea. | *We booked accommodation for a week by the sea. | We booked accommodations of the sea for a week. | We booked an accommodation of sea for a week.
